# Verify that -rewrite keeps weak undefined dynamic symbols undefined on
# AArch64 when linked with GNU ld.
#
# GNU ld gives weak undefined functions a non-zero st_value in .dynsym
# pointing at their PLT stub (e.g. the C++ personality routine
# __gxx_personality_v0; lld leaves the value zero, so this variant needs
# bfd). -rewrite used to rewrite such an entry into a *defined* symbol in
# the .plt section: the dynamic linker searches the main executable
# first, resolved the symbol's JUMP_SLOT to the local PLT stub, and the
# first throw then spun forever in a PLT self-loop (the stub jumps back
# through the very GOT slot being resolved).
#
# With the fix the entry stays undefined, the JUMP_SLOT resolves to the
# real implementation in libstdc++, and the rewritten binary prints the
# regular catch output.

# REQUIRES: gnu_ld

# RUN: %clangxx %cxxflags -g -O1 -Wl,-q -no-pie -fuse-ld=bfd \
# RUN:   %S/Inputs/rewrite-exceptions.cpp -o %t.orig
## Sanity-check the input shape: undefined entry with a non-zero value.
# RUN: llvm-readelf --dyn-syms %t.orig | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECK-INPUT
# CHECK-INPUT: UND __gxx_personality_v0
# RUN: llvm-bolt %t.orig -o %t.bolt -rewrite
# RUN: llvm-readelf --dyn-syms %t.bolt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECK-DYNSYM
# CHECK-DYNSYM: UND __gxx_personality_v0
# RUN: %t.bolt | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: catch 2
# CHECK: catch 1
# CHECK: caught ExcC
